Package: llmmetric
Title: Psychometric Validation and Inference for LLM-Coded Data
Version: 0.5.2
Authors@R: 
    person(
      given = "Marcus",
      family = "Harris",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      email = "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com"
    )
Description: Treats large language models (LLMs) explicitly as fallible
    measurement instruments for quantitative research data. Orchestrates
    reproducible multi-facet coding designs with resumable checkpointing,
    integrity-checked disk caching, strict JSON schema validation, and
    pluggable 'OpenAI'-compatible, local 'Ollama', custom R callable, or
    deterministic mock backends; estimates Generalizability Theory variance
    components and D-study reliability projections (Brennan, 2001,
    ISBN:978-0-387-95282-6), calibration against human gold standards and
    inter-rater reliability ceilings, temporal drift, and Differential Prompt
    Functioning (DPF); implements stratified/active validation sampling and
    Prediction-Powered Inference (PPI, PPI++, Horvitz-Thompson IPW-PPI,
    cross-fitted non-linear calibration, category prevalences, and clustered
    or multilevel extensions; Angelopoulos et al., 2023
    <doi:10.1126/science.adi6000>) alongside validation sample-size planning,
    APA reporting tables, and 'ggplot2' diagnostic visualizations.
